course: dictionary
lesson: 528
title: Who studies the sky?
level: primary-5
stars: 0
explain: An astronomer is a scientist who studies the stars, planets, moons, comets and galaxies. Astronomers look at everything in space, not just the sky above your house.
explain: Read the clues in the sentence: «Astronomers have found more than 6,000 planets around other stars.» Planets and stars are things in space, and found tells you that astronomers look carefully and count what they see.
explain: The word is built from two parts. Astro comes from a Greek word meaning star, and -er means a person who does something. A teacher teaches, so an astronomer studies stars. You can be one too: an amateur astronomer watches the night sky as a hobby.
fact: An astronomer is a scientist who studies space.
fact: Astronomers use telescopes, satellites and computers.
fact: «Pluto was discovered in 1930 by Clyde Tombaugh, a young American astronomer.»
fact: Galileo used an early telescope to see the moons of Jupiter.
fact: An amateur astronomer watches the night sky as a hobby, for example by spotting constellations and the Moon's phases.
exercise: «Astronomers have found more than 6,000 planets around other stars.» What do astronomers study? | *Stars, planets and other things in space | Cakes and biscuits | Only the weather on Earth | Old coins from long ago
exercise: «Galaxies spin so fast that their visible stars and gas cannot hold them together.» Find and copy one word that names something in space. | *galaxies | visible | spin | ordinary
exercise: What is an amateur astronomer? | A teacher of maths | *A person who watches the night sky as a hobby, often with a telescope | A cook who makes star-shaped biscuits | A pilot who flies planes at night
test: Which of these is a tool that astronomers use? | Hammer | Paintbrush | Spoon | *Telescope
test: «Just a hundred years ago many astronomers thought our Milky Way was the whole universe.» What did astronomers once think the Milky Way was? | The Moon's shadow | A type of telescope | *The whole universe | A small planet
exam: Who said that the Earth goes round the Sun? | Edwin Hubble | Galileo | *Copernicus | Clyde Tombaugh
